    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d655">

                <pb facs="0917" n="811" xml:id="pg811"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Jackson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-07-17"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 112.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I confirm the text of the department’s
                    telegram of the 13th instant to Mr. Wilson.<anchor n="a" xml:id="d655-f1"/></p>
                <p>I inclose herewith, in further response to your dispatches referred to in the
                    above-quoted telegram, copies of letters from the Secretary of Commerce and
                    Labor pointing out, for the information of the Greek minister for foreign
                    affairs, the provisions of law applicable to the cases of deported Greek
                    emigrants on which the minister’s inquiries are based.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d655-a1.xml" xpointer="d655-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d655-a2.xml" xpointer="d655-a2"/>
            </div>
